The  file specifies which are sets of tuples that are to be given
similar network access.  Each line in the file consists of a net‐
group name followed by a list of the  members  of  the  netgroup.
Each member can be either the name of another netgroup or a spec‐
ification  of  a tuple as follows: (host, user, domain) where the
and are character string names for the  corresponding  component.
Any of the comma separated fields may be empty to specify a value
or  may  consist of the string to specify The members of the list
may be separated by whitespace; the character may be used at  the
end of a line to specify line continuation.  The functions speci‐
fied  in  should  normally be used to access the database.  If is
specified for the database in (or no entry  is  specified),  then
these  functions  operate on the version of the file which can be
generated using If is specified  then  the  maps  and  are  used.
